From 8ca95073998481973f3ab80e3436178bbd2f7145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <huhuvmb88@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:14:17 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: ROCKET_FS_MIDZERO, zero the slice between
 A/B/C and the tail

With the vendor tail grafted, everything from 0x0b90 on is byte identical
between models, conv2d-cal computes correctly and cal_k3 is still flat at the
zero point, so the kernel dependence is not in the tail. What is left is 0x400
to 0x0b90, holding the first 1936 bytes of the float surface.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
index 0bd2298..5debdb8 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
@@ -745,6 +745,19 @@ rkt_fill_biases(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
        * are not needed and the buffer is far simpler than assumed. If it breaks,
        * the vendor's structure cannot be grafted on piecemeal.
        */
+      /*
+       * ROCKET_FS_MIDZERO: zero the slice between the A/B/C table and the tail.
+       *
+       * With the tail grafted, everything from 0x0b90 on is byte identical
+       * between models, conv2d-cal is correct and cal_k3 is still flat at the
+       * zero point, so the kernel dependence is not in the tail. What is left
+       * k-dependent in this buffer is 0x400 to 0x0b90, still holding the first
+       * 1936 bytes of the float surface. Zeroing exactly that slice says
+       * whether the buffer carries the dependence at all.
+       */
+      if (getenv("ROCKET_FS_MIDZERO") && bufsize > 0x0b90)
+         memset(b8 + 0x400, 0, 0x0b90 - 0x400);
+
       const char *tailf = getenv("ROCKET_FS_TAIL");
       if (tailf && bufsize > 0x0b90) {
          FILE *f = fopen(tailf, "rb");
-- 
